{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals","id":1120687,"title":"Archmages Vs Other Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-26T00:34:56-07:00","id":1120687,"title":"Archmages Vs Other Supernaturals","content":"I was wondering, are any of the other supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, demons, etc.) capable of taking on archmages? I'm of course talking about the more powerful members with power stats at 6+ dots and lots of their respective powers . If so, which ones are and which ones aren't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T00:52:30-07:00","id":1120693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals#post1120687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, are any of the other supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, demons, etc.) capable of taking on archmages? I'm of course talking about the more powerful members with power stats at 6+ dots and lots of their respective powers . If so, which ones are and which ones aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Archmasters aren't just Gnosis 6+, they're essentially a modifed template quite distinct to normal magi. The usual formulation is an archmaster is to a mage as a mage is to a sleeper.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:10:03-07:00","id":1120737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals#post1120687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, are any of the other supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, demons, etc.) capable of taking on archmages? I'm of course talking about the more powerful members with power stats at 6+ dots and lots of their respective powers . If so, which ones are and which ones aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is talk in the 1e Imperial Mysteries book of sponsor entities who rival Archmasters in power that protect the various other supers from Archmasters tampering but they arnt stat'd. Rank 6+ spirits have imperial magic like abilities in their respective influences, so they can probably hold their own vs a unprepared Archmaster who hasnt managed to prepare for a IM spell.<br /> <br /> Any playable template has no real hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:39:09-07:00","id":1120772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals#post1120687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, are any of the other supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, demons, etc.) capable of taking on archmages? I'm of course talking about the more powerful members with power stats at 6+ dots and lots of their respective powers . If so, which ones are and which ones aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have an archmaster as the antagonist of a chronicle, focusing on twarting the gathering of quintessences for his imperial spells and thus the agents he uses to subvert the pax arcana subtly. In a straight conflict? without fiat such as the sponsorship of the above mentioned entities or other opposed archmasters using your characters as their own agents, the conflict would boil down to being obliterated by imperial praxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:09:41-07:00","id":1121444,"title":"","content":"What would an Arch master level Chronicle even look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:43:02-07:00","id":1121463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121444#post1121444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would an Arch master level Chronicle even look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobilis? Stuff blowing up? Wiki wars (but with reality)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:11:31-07:00","id":1121523,"title":"","content":"There are Incarnate Beasts, who are the archmage equivalent of the Beast line, and in the werewolf settings of the core book there is a werewolf that was able to be the totem of a lodge, so I believe it is implied that he reached a similar level of power.<br /> <br /> I thought the vampire Methuselahs in 1000 years of night was going to be their equivalent, but that wasn't actually the case. I also remember in the Book of the Dead a sineater was starting to become a Kerborei (I just know that is spelled wrong). Not sure about changelings and the other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:33:49-07:00","id":1121544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121523#post1121523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Incarnate Beasts, who are the archmage equivalent of the Beast line, and in the werewolf settings of the core book there is a werewolf that was able to be the totem of a lodge, so I believe it is implied that he reached a similar level of power.<br /> <br /> I thought the vampire Methuselahs in 1000 years of night was going to be their equivalent, but that wasn't actually the case. I also remember in the Book of the Dead a sineater was starting to become a Kerborei (I just know that is spelled wrong). Not sure about changelings and the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I know that in 1E a changeling could potentially become a True Fae if they got Wyrd 10 and went to the Hedge, so I suppose that would be their equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T19:50:13-07:00","id":1121675,"title":"","content":"Before counting Elder Vampires out remember this: Nothing in Imperial Mysteries says Archmasters can't be blood bound. <br /> <br /> Also fun side note: A personal favorite fan theory if mine is that the Fog of Eternity isn't so much Kindred Elders going senile, but Elders retaining the memory of their previous incarnations before an Archmage reality edits. That way it seems like they remember things that didn't happen, but really they're remembering things that no longer happened. Fun food for thought. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T19:55:50-07:00","id":1121676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121675#post1121675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before counting Elder Vampires out remember this: Nothing in Imperial Mysteries says Archmasters can't be blood bound. <br /> <br /> Also fun side note: A personal favorite fan theory if mine is that the Fog of Eternity isn't so much Kindred Elders going senile, but Elders retaining the memory of their previous incarnations before an Archmage reality edits. That way it seems like they remember things that didn't happen, but really they're remembering things that no longer happened. Fun food for thought. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>This...is <i>awesome</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:00:40-07:00","id":1121677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121675#post1121675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before counting Elder Vampires out remember this: Nothing in Imperial Mysteries says Archmasters can't be blood bound. <br /> <br /> Also fun side note: A personal favorite fan theory if mine is that the Fog of Eternity isn't so much Kindred Elders going senile, but Elders retaining the memory of their previous incarnations before an Archmage reality edits. That way it seems like they remember things that didn't happen, but really they're remembering things that no longer happened. Fun food for thought. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting mages can clear the blood bond though. So, an Archmage, while fully capable of being under the bond, would not be under the bond soon after the bond occurred unless they chose to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:22:30-07:00","id":1121682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121677#post1121677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Starting mages can clear the blood bond though. So, an Archmage, while fully capable of being under the bond, would not be under the bond soon after the bond occurred unless they chose to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if it was part of a Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:57:12-07:00","id":1121695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121682#post1121682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine if it was part of a Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how Quintessence applies to this situation. A mage can restore their pattern with three mana (which lets them clear any mental condition).<br /> <br /> And beyond that, vampires count as sleepwalkers when it comes to Supernal Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:16:23-07:00","id":1121702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121695#post1121695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how Quintessence applies to this situation. A mage can restore their pattern with three mana (which lets them clear any mental condition).<br /> <br /> And beyond that, vampires count as sleepwalkers when it comes to Supernal Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Malus is pointing out that chances are, if a vampire managed to blood bond an Archmage, it was honestly probably part of the archmages plan to be blood bond from the start in order to use that as Quintessence for an Imperial Spell of some sort. That and that that would make a pretty awesome excuse for one to let it ride for a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T22:43:34-07:00","id":1121724,"title":"","content":"That wouldn't work as per 2e where they're basically immune to everything lower than another 6+ entity. It would also be over the minute they left to the golden road and basically get rid of their body if they didn't already clear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-28-2017, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T22:49:28-07:00","id":1121726,"title":"","content":"That's not a bad idea, and just the sort of thing an Archmage would get up too. <br /> <br /> I'd personally, run the Blood Bond the same way I'd run it if a regular Mage got the Vinculum. They CAN easily remove the blood bond, but due to the sinister nature of the bond would they WANT to if it was servers enough. Either way, perfect excuse to have the Mage/Archmaster battle the Vinculumn Goetia in the Astral Realm am I right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Shit, that's right. Their body is Astral in origin now that they're bound to the Golden Road...but wait. Can't Kindred potentially Blood Bind Ghosts, Spirits, and other Emphemeral entities of they're manifested? The Cure is a metaphysical condition, so as long as the Kindred is Blood Potency 6+ then is there a chance it's still possible?. Could very well be wrong though...damn, so much for epic Vinculum Goetia battle... :,(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-28-2017, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T00:45:09-07:00","id":1121746,"title":"","content":"The Blood Bond is a metaphysical condition, I assume it would transcend the limitation of a physical body no longer existing. It's easily dealt with by Space 3 though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T00:57:49-07:00","id":1121749,"title":"","content":"Phew, that's good to hear. *fishes idea out of trash bin* <br /> <br /> And yes, my point was that it is easy to remove it*. But removing it while under it's effects would be a little more difficult that I feel is being acknowledged. Nothing stopping someone who isn't under the bond from helping someone else out though, just that I kinda feel that would be a wasted opportunity for Beats and possible Arcane Beats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *That being said, the Vinculum isn't exactly the same as a sympathetic connection. I feel there is creative room for the storyteller to make interesting plot hooks around removing the Vinculum without just magicing it away. For one example, the Space 3 spell works until slowly the Blood Bond returns within a number of nights. Turns out the bond was successfully removed, but the lingering Vitae and subsistent Curse remained within their system unchanged and now must be delt with another way. (Death or Life Arcana anyone...or Vinculum Goetia battle!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T01:23:19-07:00","id":1121752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121695#post1121695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how Quintessence applies to this situation. A mage can restore their pattern with three mana (which lets them clear any mental condition).<br /> <br /> And beyond that, vampires count as sleepwalkers when it comes to Supernal Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the thingh though, it let them clear any Mental Condition (with a upper case C). One could argue that things like Dominated is a supernatural Condition and not a Mental one.<br /> But then again, being blood bound ain't technically a Condition. So Pattern Restoration is out of the question. <br /> However it's still easy to get rid of the bond with quite low spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T02:09:21-07:00","id":1121755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121752#post1121752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again, being blood bound ain't technically a Condition. So Pattern Restoration is out of the question.<br /> However it's still easy to get rid of the bond with quite low spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was basically going to point out this bit. There is no 'Blood Bound' Condition - or at least, not that I can find. Under the assumption that the state of being Blood Bound is not registered as a Condition, I would actually make a case that - barring the use of actual spells - it would not be among the natural capabilities of an Awakened Mage's Template to remove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T03:39:09-07:00","id":1121769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121749#post1121749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*That being said, the Vinculum isn't exactly the same as a sympathetic connection. I feel there is creative room for the storyteller</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually is, it's been a long established fact that the never published legacy the Tamers of Blood which are a Space primary legacy are experts in removing the the blood bond. It functions pretty much exactly like a strong Sympathetic connection as well.<br /> <br /> That being said, there is more than one way to skin a cat and the ST does have creative room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T07:02:45-07:00","id":1121817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121726#post1121726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a bad idea, and just the sort of thing an Archmage would get up too.<br /> <br /> I'd personally, run the Blood Bond the same way I'd run it if a regular Mage got the Vinculum. They CAN easily remove the blood bond, but due to the sinister nature of the bond would they WANT to if it was servers enough. Either way, perfect excuse to have the Mage/Archmaster battle the Vinculumn Goetia in the Astral Realm am I right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Shit, that's right. Their body is Astral in origin now that they're bound to the Golden Road...but wait. Can't Kindred potentially Blood Bind Ghosts, Spirits, and other Emphemeral entities of they're manifested? The Cure is a metaphysical condition, so as long as the Kindred is Blood Potency 6+ then is there a chance it's still possible?. Could very well be wrong though...damn, so much for epic Vinculum Goetia battle... :,(</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank six does not mean powerstat six. a normal mage at gnosis ten could never compete with an archmaster. You need a higher level template to compete with archmasters who are literally on another playing field.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:55:34-07:00","id":1121886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121749#post1121749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phew, that's good to hear. *fishes idea out of trash bin*<br /> <br /> And yes, my point was that it is easy to remove it*. But removing it while under it's effects would be a little more difficult that I feel is being acknowledged. Nothing stopping someone who isn't under the bond from helping someone else out though, just that I kinda feel that would be a wasted opportunity for Beats and possible Arcane Beats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *That being said, the Vinculum isn't exactly the same as a sympathetic connection. I feel there is creative room for the storyteller to make interesting plot hooks around removing the Vinculum without just magicing it away. For one example, the Space 3 spell works until slowly the Blood Bond returns within a number of nights. Turns out the bond was successfully removed, but the lingering Vitae and subsistent Curse remained within their system unchanged and now must be delt with another way. (Death or Life Arcana anyone...or Vinculum Goetia battle!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, considering how mages (nevermind their ascended kin) are prone to their obsession bits, becoming obsessed with one's regnant to the point of not undoing said vinculum seems perfectly feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:58:57-07:00","id":1121923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121769#post1121769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually is, it's been a long established fact that the never published legacy the Tamers of Blood which are a Space primary legacy are experts in removing the the blood bond. It functions pretty much exactly like a strong Sympathetic connection as well.<br /> <br /> That being said, there is more than one way to skin a cat and the ST does have creative room.</div> </div> </div> </div>...wait, so you're baseing this theory on a 1st Edition Legacy that was never published?<br /> <br /> You know what, more power too you. If the material adds something to your game setting then it's perfectly acceptable. <br /> <br /> In fact that's probably the logic that sums up the whole discussion. Not every game of Mage is going to use the same metaphysical concepts, so talk it out with your players first and if they like it them feel free to use it. You can always blame it on some Archmaster anyways. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-28-2017, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:45:19-07:00","id":1121956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121923#post1121923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...wait, so you're baseing this theory on a 1st Edition Legacy that was never published?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is mentioned again in the legacy section of the 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not basing it on that, I'm using that as a support for the argument that the blood bond is a sympathetic connection. The actual base is that it acts just like an artificially strengthened connection creating obsession in the bonded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T11:06:04-07:00","id":1121965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121956#post1121956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I'm not basing it on that, I'm using that as a support for the argument that the blood bond is a sympathetic connection. The actual base is that it acts just like an artificially strengthened connection creating obsession in the bonded.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically basing your argument on a source that hasn't been published yet. It's a chicken or egg argument: does intimacy produces sympathy? does sympathy produces intimacy? I'd lean on &quot;yes&quot; in both accounts. Few things are as intimate for a vampire as to sharing their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T11:42:17-07:00","id":1121976,"title":"","content":"I don't know what your actual point is. It appears you're just agreeing with me, am I getting that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T06:40:04-07:00","id":1124278,"title":"","content":"Seems more likely he's claiming that a group that magically manipulates sympathy through blood ties having the ability to manipulate a vampire blood bond isn't great evidence that a blood bond is just a sympathetic bond.<br /> <br /> All blood bonds having sympathy doesn't imply that sympathy is what they are, nor that they can be trivially removed with Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T09:32:58-07:00","id":1124337,"title":"","content":"I've kind of always looked at Archmages as the in game meta-&quot;Story Tellers&quot;. They are the reason vampires exist, or the Strix, or the Werewolves et cet. They are the end game boss before the secret bonus fight, the God Machine itself which organizes the world as I see fit. Aswadim could easily be using vampires or strix to harvest bits for their imperial spells. Werewolves are very explainable by the lens of a Thyrsus Archmage even with their own myths. I'm not 100% certain, but I've structured my game based on the assumption that mage is pretty much the most powerful splat and the fluff arranges itself around that or perhaps it's vice-versa and the fluff makes its mechanics so strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13727,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13727-totallynotatremere","user":"TotallyNotaTremere","date":".  grammarz 08-03-2017, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13727-totallynotatremere","name":"TotallyNotaTremere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13727_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:41:25-07:00","id":1124503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TotallyNotaTremere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124337#post1124337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've kind of always looked at Archmages as the in game meta-&amp;quot;Story Tellers&amp;quot;. They are the reason vampires exist, or the Strix, or the Werewolves et cet. They are the end game boss before the secret bonus fight, the God Machine itself which organizes the world as I see fit. Aswadim could easily be using vampires or strix to harvest bits for their imperial spells. Werewolves are very explainable by the lens of a Thyrsus Archmage even with their own myths. I'm not 100% certain, but I've structured my game based on the assumption that mage is pretty much the most powerful splat and the fluff arranges itself around that or perhaps it's vice-versa and the fluff makes its mechanics so strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was stated in the Archmage book that each of the supernaturals, like vampires and werewolves and such, have some kind of higher beings representing them in the ascension war. I think it'd be more likely that those beings were responsible for making them. Also, I don't really know how long ago the first mages were supposed to have appeared, but from what I've heard there may have been vampires or vampire-like creatures since the beginning of human civilization, possibly long before it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:51:07-07:00","id":1124507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124503#post1124503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it was stated in the Archmage book that each of the supernaturals, like vampires and werewolves and such, have some kind of higher beings representing them in the ascension war. I think it'd be more likely that those beings were responsible for making them. Also, I don't really know how long ago the first mages were supposed to have appeared, but from what I've heard there may have been vampires or vampire-like creatures since the beginning of human civilization, possibly long before it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it not also hinted that vampires might be the result of a death archmaster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:57:39-07:00","id":1124510,"title":"","content":"I've never been a particular fan of making Archmages the reasons the other splats were around; partially because &quot;A wizard did it&quot; feels like the boring option. <br /> <br /> Vampires themselves have different origin stories for each clan, and werewolves have the Father Wolf tale. Just tossing that stuff out and just pointing at old archmages just seems, to me at least, like you're tossing out a lot of the stuff you can use from those splats mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:00:09-07:00","id":1124512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124507#post1124507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is it not also hinted that vampires might be the result of a death archmaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I've mostly only read the mechanics out of the book, most of what I know about vampire history I've heard from other people. I do know that when I made a thread about how old vampires as a species were, many people thought they at least dated back to the Neolithic period, and Rose Bailey actually stated that they were as old as humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:03:59-07:00","id":1124515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124503#post1124503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't really know how long ago the first mages were supposed to have appeared, but from what I've heard there may have been vampires or vampire-like creatures since the beginning of human civilization, possibly long before it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If an Archmage changes the Supernal to have vampires exist, they would retroactively have always existed.<br /> <br /> Not something I'd do in a crossover setting, but if I wanted to run a pure Mage game with everything being Mage-centric it could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:07:00-07:00","id":1124517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124512#post1124512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I've mostly only read the mechanics out of the book, most of what I know about vampire history I've heard from other people. I do know that when I made a thread about how old vampires as a species were, many people thought they at least dated back to the Neolithic period, and Rose Bailey actually stated that they were as old as humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If vampires were1 created by a archmaster it could happen retrospectively and they would have always been around. Some archmage might have just created them yesterday in reality but as far as the rest of the world is concerned they have been around since the dawn of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:12:43-07:00","id":1124521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124517#post1124517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If vampires were1 created by a archmaster it could happen retrospectively and they would have always been around. Some archmage might have just created them yesterday in reality but as far as the rest of the world is concerned they have been around since the dawn of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't there usually other beings that oppose mages making massive changes to the world? Creating an entirely new species which would influence and bend mortal society to their whims for tens of thousands of years seems like it might stir up a bit of controversy among the other supernal beings and Archmages, don't you think? Out of all of the creatures an Archmage could retcon into existence, vampires seem like one of the least likely ones for them to get away with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 08-03-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:20:24-07:00","id":1124523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124521#post1124521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't there usually other beings that oppose mages making massive changes to the world? Creating an entirely new species which would influence and bend mortal society to their whims for tens of thousands of years seems like it might stir up a bit of controversy among the other supernal beings and Archmages, don't you think? Out of all of the creatures an Archmage could retcon into existence, vampires seem like one of the least likely ones for them to get away with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could have happened before the pax was formed, or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:29:27-07:00","id":1124525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124523#post1124523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Could have happened before the pax was formed, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Was there a time before the Pax? Regardless, whether there was a Pax or not wouldn't that still have pissed something off? There doesn't need to be a Pax for powerful beings to get upset at others making huge changes to the world. Wasn't the Pax just formed so that they wouldn't start massive destructive wars over it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:46:57-07:00","id":1124531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124525#post1124525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Was there a time before the Pax? Regardless, whether there was a Pax or not wouldn't that still have pissed something off? There doesn't need to be a Pax for powerful beings to get upset at others making huge changes to the world. Wasn't the Pax just formed so that they wouldn't start massive destructive wars over it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was probably a time when archmasters were in massive destructive wars with gods, each other and stuff, maybe just after some of them got kicked out of the supernal and decided they needed the pax to stop the chaos. As far as i remember from IM only other archmasters who are in their golden road at the time the fallen world is edited are aware of any changes made to the fallen world should they ever return to it? As for anything non Archmaster then they would have been altered aswell to assume that vampires had always existed so why would it piss them off, they prob dont even know a archmaster was responsible? Other archmasters might get pissed and thats what the pax is about, there was hints that christianity is the result of a archmaster mistake that overwrite the old mithrian religion and that archmaster has promised to fix it, Perhaps a archmaster has promised to fix his creation of vampires but has trouble because now they have a powerful spirit that protects them?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T17:23:30-07:00","id":1124537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124531#post1124531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> There was probably a time when archmasters were in massive destructive wars with gods, each other and stuff, maybe just after some of them got kicked out of the supernal and decided they needed the pax to stop the chaos. As far as i remember from IM only other archmasters who are in their golden road at the time the fallen world is edited are aware of any changes made to the fallen world should they ever return to it? As for anything non Archmaster then they would have been altered aswell to assume that vampires had always existed so why would it piss them off, they prob dont even know a archmaster was responsible? Other archmasters might get pissed and thats what the pax is about, there was hints that christianity is the result of a archmaster mistake that overwrite the old mithrian religion and that archmaster has promised to fix it, Perhaps a archmaster has promised to fix his creation of vampires but has trouble because now they have a powerful spirit that protects them?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When I say that other beings get pissed off, I mean things on the level of Archmages, stuff like the gods they fight and spirits at Rank 6-10. If such beings were really unaware of the changes by Archmages I don't see how they could pose a serous threat to them, yet they still wind up fighting each other. Then there is always the theory that Imperial Magic is really just the Archmage travelling to another universe where what they want to be true is true, in which case they wouldn't really be responsible for changing anything, simply bringing themselves and others to another universe.<br /> <br /> As for the Christianity thing, yeah and the Beasts think that all supernatural beings are descended from the Dark Mother, the Lancea Sanctum think they were cursed by God, the Ordo Dracul think Dracula founded their Covenant, and the werewolves have their story about Father Wolf. All the supernaturals have creation stories, and a lot of the time it has to do with them, including mages thinking that an Archmage made Christianitybor vampires, and even some supposedly thinking that the God Machine was made by an Archmage. That doesn't make any of it true, it's all rumours and stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 08-03-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T22:58:56-07:00","id":1124628,"title":"","content":"The Pax has always existed. It just hasn't always always existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T23:06:59-07:00","id":1124631,"title":"","content":"Well we at least know there was a Father Wolf, the what's and why's of it are more confusing. And Dracula did found the Ordo Dracul, though honestly I think his brides did most of the work, he was certainly a patron of their studies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:36:50-07:00","id":1124808,"title":"","content":"If I were going to run a meta-templates like Archmage is on top of the Mage template for other Templates, I'd have Golconda be the meta-template for Vampires and of equivalent power, and I only say that because no one has mention Golconda in this thread yet, despite it being listed as a state of Transcendence for a vampire, thus a vampire in how I envision Golconda would be able to Clash Wills with Arch Mages normally, for <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CapitalLettersAreMagic\" target=\"_blank\">Gaining Redemption from the pits of Damnation is as worthy and epic a goal as Ascending to Truth from a Lie</a>.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Entities already have rank 6 and above for that power level.<br /> <br /> Don't really know Changeling, Sin-Eater, Forsaken equivalent transcendent states, which is how I view Archmage-hood, a transcendent state of a Major Template.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-04-2017, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:54:12-07:00","id":1124815,"title":"","content":"We had sort of a glimpse of the Bodhisattva predator mentioned more than a few times in werewolf. There does seem to be an 'end game' aspect to them it doesn't have a book about it yet, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> One of the writers for Werewolf did offer us <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves#post801351\">a write-up on one of them</a>, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bodhisattva Predator:</b> Having transcended into something greater, Lycaon-Ur has an increased Essence Pool and Essence per turn capability. He is capable of entering the Sacred Hunt at any time without needing to perform the rite, simply gaining the Siskur-Dah Condition against a prey of his choice. He is a set part of reality and cannot be removed from it except by his death; attempts to delete Lycaon-Ur from the timeline, rewrite reality so that he is not part of it or otherwise utterly unmake him will fail.<br /> <i>Totemic Transcendence: </i>Achieved enlightenment through spiritual power, becoming a totem. Lycaon-Ur gains Influences as if he were a spirit of Rank equal to his honorary Rank, using Presence + Wits in place of Power + Finesse. He gains 3 Essence per day and 1 additional point of Influence due to serving as a totem to his Lodge. He also gains the usual capabilities of a Lodge totem to detect Lodge members, etc.<br /> <i>Enlightenments:</i> Lycaon-Ur has access to the following powers:<br /> <i>Enlightened Renown (Cunning, Glory):</i> Lycaon-Ur gains the Rote quality on all dice pools that include his Cunning or Glory Renowns.<br /> <i>Inviolate Soul:</i> Lycaon-Ur\u2019s soul cannot be damaged, tampered with or removed by anything but an idigam, and while on the Sacred Hunt no mind-influencing affects can cause him to turn from his prey.<br /> <i>Primal Form (Urshul): </i>Lycaon-Ur adds his Purity to his Strength and Size in Urshul form.<br /> <i>Radiant Flesh:</i> As well as his normal regeneration, Lycaon-Ur regenerates a single point of aggravated damage every turn.<br /> <i>Stainless Harmony: </i>Lycaon-Ur\u2019s Harmony is set at 5 and cannot change. </div> </div> </div>The obvious one for Changeling is a True Fae, something they could become in first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:26:03-07:00","id":1124825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124815#post1124815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had sort of a glimpse of the Bodhisattva predator mentioned more than a few times in werewolf. There does seem to be an 'end game' aspect to them it doesn't have a book about it yet, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> One of the writers for Werewolf did offer us <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves#post801351&amp;quot;]a</a> write-up on one of them[/URL], though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The obvious one for Changeling is a True Fae, something they could become in first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd make Eldrich Entitlements the equivilant of an Archmage and True Fae the equiviliant of an Ascended Mage.<br /> <br /> Or maybe simply allow a Changeling to steal amd use a Fae title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:54:01-07:00","id":1124861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124825#post1124825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or maybe simply allow a Changeling to steal amd use a Fae title.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that be what makes a Changeling into an Other in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:58:25-07:00","id":1124863,"title":"","content":"No, it'd still have a soul.<br /> <br /> Amyways I think some powerful Supernal beings connected to the concepts related to other Supernal Creatures might object to Archmages messing with those creatures.<br /> <br /> A Spectre related to ideas of Vampirism might object to Archmages trying to mess with a Kindreds template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:50:09-07:00","id":1125216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1124863#post1124863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it'd still have a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubt it. Pretty sure the requirement to use the title would be to become subsumed on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:41:06-07:00","id":1125241,"title":"","content":"As a matter of fact, the Pax does not absolutely stop an Archmage from making significant changes with Imperial magic to the templates of other supernaturals, either individually or for the whole spat. It only forbids them from doing so w/o the approval of the godlike patrons of the splat. One would suppose such approval may be obtained by divine bargaining. And as usual, this does not concern Imperium rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 08-05-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T11:18:49-07:00","id":1125285,"title":"","content":"I don't think vampires have a patron.<br /> <br /> Clans have been wiped out, but new ones will keep rising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T12:27:18-07:00","id":1125308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1125285#post1125285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think vampires have a patron.<br /> <br /> Clans have been wiped out, but new ones will keep rising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres being wiped out by natural fallen world (read strix) causes and then there is being wiped out by a archmaster. Clans rising and falling is a natural part of being a vampire, if a archmaster decided to remove ALL vampires then im sure the vampiric patron would step in and say &quot;Uh no&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:58:55-07:00","id":1125342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1125308#post1125308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres being wiped out by natural fallen world (read strix) causes and then there is being wiped out by a archmaster. Clans rising and falling is a natural part of being a vampire, if a archmaster decided to remove ALL vampires then im sure the vampiric patron would step in and say &quot;Uh no&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires aren't sure what happened to the Julii. Some may blame the strix, but they don't know about archmages. They all disappeared in one fell swoop. Even if you got rid of all vampires, some would pop up again in a new form. You already have them. The Jiang-shi, the ghul, the Formosae and Penanggalan and the list goes on and on. At its heart it's such a basic idea. Something is back from the dead. To sustain its undeath, it needs life. You already have it in a lesser form with ghosts, who need life's attention.<br /> <br /> But again, don't think there's a vampiric patron. Though I'm sure there's high beings that don't want the world disrupted that much. You don't have to be an environmentalist to want to stop some mad bastard from committing genocide on some species or another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:28:07-07:00","id":1125350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1125342#post1125342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But again, don't think there's a vampiric patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tend to agree on principle, but Imperial Mysteries outright states that they do.<br /> <br /> It does however read like something put in to stop people arguing on the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:45:45-07:00","id":1125358,"title":"","content":"I could see Supernal Entities tied to vampiric concepts and Ancient Strix, far more powerful then what appears in the core, as patrons for vampires, and maybe weirder things too, like the Crone and Longinus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:51:30-07:00","id":1125361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1125350#post1125350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would tend to agree on principle, but Imperial Mysteries outright states that they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having <i>a </i>patron isn't really contradicted by having patron<i>s</i> \u2014 vampirism is sufficiently nonuniform that messing around with entrenched and/or widespread groups of vampires is going to be met with resistance by some amount of potent sponsorship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:25:54-07:00","id":1125383,"title":"","content":"Yes, the book doesn't say everyone has a unique patron, or that the patron is even related to the template. 'All supernatural beings with greater templates and some with lesser templates have sponsors in the Ascension War who actively prevent archmages from meddling with their agents.' And as Satchel points out, anyone could have a stake in vampires existing, they have their uses.<br /> <br /> If an ancient all-powerful strix were around, it would likely not be a patron, it would actively seek to upend them. The strix don't like vampires, they like tormenting vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T18:55:11-07:00","id":1125447,"title":"","content":"The 'patron' of the Kindred might not be anything <i>remotely</i> related to the undead. A sinister enough archmage might have taken a fancy to them, and now's 'looking out for them' out of a twisted sense of affection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T08:41:12-07:00","id":1125607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1125361#post1125361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not having <i>a </i>patron isn't really contradicted by having patron<i>s</i> \u2014 vampirism is sufficiently nonuniform that messing around with entrenched and/or widespread groups of vampires is going to be met with resistance by some amount of potent sponsorship.</div> </div> </div> </div>The supernal concept of vampirism sound adequate enough to prevent wholly undue alteration to it's state of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T09:04:53-07:00","id":1125609,"title":"","content":"In my personal headcanon vampires (as far as MtAw games are concerned, I wouldn't run it that way in a VtR game) have been created by the Psychopomp as a means of stifling humanities potential to awaken. Vampires still have souls, but they're crippled things, unable to awaken and they infect those they feed upon with a little bit of themselves. Sure you can still awaken even if you're being fed from regularily by vampires but in my personal headcanon the chances decrease (and are really small for ghouls).<br /> <br /> Therefore a possible patron would be one of the Iron Seals itself... and then there're allways the Strix themselves who probably came from some sort of lower depth. Maybe they've been invited by the Psychopomp or maybe they're an independent faction, hard to say. But truly powerful Striga could exsist, though it's questionable wether they can pass over into the phenomenal world (without breaking it horribly first).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:36:56-07:00","id":1125679,"title":"","content":"The Principle would logically be the Prometheans' godlike 'sponsor'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T14:44:23-07:00","id":1125695,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel like any particular blood god might have a vested interest in sponsoring vampiric activity in the world. And of course, said blood gods are not the only possible patrons - Archmages who are curious about the very nature of vampirism who have yet to study them might be upset at their being altered. Certain Tetrarchs and Exarches might well be interested in keeping the vampires because they push - even unknowingly - the Lie. It's been mentioned that godlike strix might well be interested in their continued torment.<br /> <br /> And even if all of these potential groups might not be willing to back and support the vampires, and the vampires are the poor lonely orphans of the Ascension War - they can always find cold solace in the bosom of the Dark Mother. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:11:27-07:00","id":1126343,"title":"","content":"You know, since I thought about it over the weekend, I had an idea related to my previous observation that Transcendence to a higher state of being is the thread linking the meta-templates like Archmage or the Bodhisattva Predator, or Golconda Vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>The thoughts go like this:</b><br /> What would be a Transcendent State for the Lost? Being 'Found', of course is what popped to mind. What does it mean to &quot;find one's self&quot; in a truly transcendent way? Something about finding one's place in the world, making piece with it and accepting it as a profound metaphysical truth, probably through some hero's journey or coming of age story revealing something meaningfully real and surreal at the same time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:21:54-07:00","id":1126448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1126343#post1126343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, since I thought about it over the weekend, I had an idea related to my previous observation that Transcendence to a higher state of being is the thread linking the meta-templates like Archmage or the Bodhisattva Predator, or Golconda Vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>The thoughts go like this:</b><br /> What would be a Transcendent State for the Lost? Being 'Found', of course is what popped to mind. What does it mean to &amp;quot;find one's self&amp;quot; in a truly transcendent way? Something about finding one's place in the world, making piece with it and accepting it as a profound metaphysical truth, probably through some hero's journey or coming of age story revealing something meaningfully real and surreal at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Golconda still a thing in VtR? I know it was a thing in Masquerade, but I don't think it was mentioned at all in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:35:41-07:00","id":1126455,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken it was mentioned in the 1E core book and pretty quickly dropped after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:38:14-07:00","id":1126542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1126448#post1126448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Golconda still a thing in VtR? I know it was a thing in Masquerade, but I don't think it was mentioned at all in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't seem to find it in the 2E book, so I assume they scrapped it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:53:36-07:00","id":1126548,"title":"","content":"I think that it as some sort of holy end-game for all vampires is out. But the same thing is basically the goal of the Ordo Dracul, all the power, none of the drawbacks. It's just other covenants would like different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:19:00-07:00","id":1128183,"title":"","content":"In my personal Mage canon, there is a Supernal protector of Vampires... Caine. Vampires know about his existence and worship him as the Dark Father and First Vampire, not knowing his true nature. Attempts to wipe vampires out will met not only his resistance, but also resistance of Exarchs, with whom Caine is co-existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:41:31-07:00","id":1128311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1128183#post1128183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my personal Mage canon, there is a Supernal protector of Vampires... Caine. Vampires know about his existence and worship him as the Dark Father and First Vampire, not knowing his true nature. Attempts to wipe vampires out will met not only his resistance, but also resistance of Exarchs, with whom Caine is co-existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue otherwise, but considering the Cainite heresy is a thing and the fact that I love references and callbacks to Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Though that does give me an idea for a vampiric cult. ;p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T03:30:15-07:00","id":1128379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1128311#post1128311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue otherwise, but considering the Cainite heresy is a thing and the fact that I love references and callbacks to Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just love idea of Caine. That's literally the only thing I love about Masquerade, so I decided to carry it over. Of course, it isn't regarded as the only true way; there is a ton of myths about vampire origins... but it just turns out that Cainites are right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T13:04:14-07:00","id":1132368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals#post1120687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, are any of the other supernaturals (vampires, werewolves, demons, etc.) capable of taking on archmages? I'm of course talking about the more powerful members with power stats at 6+ dots and lots of their respective powers . If so, which ones are and which ones aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my two cents if you are talking about archmages tier... <br /> True Fae, ancient powerful spirits above rank 5, totem gods like the tribal progenitors of the tribes, and probably the God machine himself or abyssal entities like the prince of 10000 leaves (from Boston unveiled)<br /> <br /> Too bad that ancient elder vampires as written are simply... Underwhelming to say the least, I thought they would get amazing powers or boost but as they are right now, they are simply of little or no concern to archmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 08-21-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:26:38-07:00","id":1133244,"title":"","content":"FWIW. I view the sponsors as not equivalent to an enhanced template of each splat. I view them as conceptually aligned to a splat. Meaning that the supernal alteration that would eliminate one of the splats also weakens or eliminates that sponsor.<br /> <br /> For example, the Quiescence to create the Mysterium, destroyed sleeper and Awakened organizations. Or, Eliminated the idea of a vampiric blood sucker, may destroy/weaken Leech gods, natural bats, and predatorily urges (affecting Werewolves too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:19:21-07:00","id":1133254,"title":"","content":"...these sponsors might also consist of archmasters. Who knows? A shamanic archmaster may be fond of Uratha and look out for them, while a Tremere archmage might view vampires as 'his'. And so forth...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T23:28:21-07:00","id":1133291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133254#post1133254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...these sponsors might also consist of archmasters. Who knows? A shamanic archmaster may be fond of Uratha and look out for them, while a Tremere archmage might view vampires as 'his'. And so forth...!</div> </div> </div> </div>An Archmaster &quot;sponsor&quot; to Uratha would more likely be a thrall to the inscrutable whims of Luna than a free agent, IMO. And he needs not be aware of so. Same for other so perceived supernatural sponsors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:01:03-07:00","id":1133401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133291#post1133291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Archmaster &quot;sponsor&quot; to Uratha would more likely be a thrall to the inscrutable whims of Luna than a free agent, IMO. And he needs not be aware of so. Same for other so perceived supernatural sponsors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? On the level that sponsor entities are they'd be at the level where a contest with Luna wouldn't be &quot;you loose&quot; automatically anymore. So sooner or later they'd see their strings, if Luna was pulling them. Not saying there aren't rank 6+ spirits or archmasters serving luna, I'm sure there are (at least the former), but I'm pretty sure these vast entities are more than just hapless victims dancing cluelessly to her viles. More like valued vassals or dupes who will be a real fucking problem if they ever find out they've been used. So probably more of the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:33:18-07:00","id":1133443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133401#post1133401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh? On the level that sponsor entities are they'd be at the level where a contest with Luna wouldn't be &quot;you loose&quot; automatically anymore. So sooner or later they'd see their strings, if Luna was pulling them. Not saying there aren't rank 6+ spirits or archmasters serving luna, I'm sure there are (at least the former), but I'm pretty sure these vast entities are more than just hapless victims dancing cluelessly to her viles. More like valued vassals or dupes who will be a real fucking problem if they ever find out they've been used. So probably more of the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, ascension isn't an &quot;I win&quot; button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:40:07-07:00","id":1133446,"title":"","content":"No, but Archmages are still super powerful entities. No need to defend other splats in the Mage forum. It gets old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T11:33:06-07:00","id":1133470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133443#post1133443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, ascension isn't an &quot;I win&quot; button.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... it sort of is? It really depends on the type of ascension and for most types its just kind of a plot device. Only for archmages who complete their omens we do have a system. And changing lunas nature/killing her probably would be like a level 4, maybe 5 omen. Level 5 omens are stuff like destroy the whole earth. Archmages don't fuck around with their goals, that said no they don't automatically win because they're Archmasters. They're just crazy enough to try shit like this... and powerful enough that when they play their cards smart they might just pull it off. Their goals are grand, their hubris transcends even legends.<br /> <br /> That said what I initially really wanted to say in response to this post: Archmasters aren't ascended. I think they are sometimes described as half ascended due to their ability to interact with the supernal in the form of Imperium Rites (which is honestly a holy shit scary ability), but otherwise they're just more powerful mages still trapped in the fallen for most of the time as they can only stand small doses of the supernal. Even their level 6+ Arcana are rooted in the fallen world only drawing down supernal symbolism into the fallen (though their level 9 power arguably could be seen as a semi short time ascension... though they still don't really make an imprint upon the supernal with that, so its still a fallen world power.)<br /> <br /> So in the end noone was ever talking about ascended beings here. Just extremly powerful gods (at least rank 6 ephemeral beings, likely higher. For example you could see the Aeons as the patrons of the individual Arcana and they're rank 8 beings I believe) and Archmages (who can rise to similar heights of power). Now I'm honestly not too versed in CofD Spirit cosmology (more knowledgable about owod, have mostly dealt with mage in CofD), no idea what exact rank Luna is. What I was saying is that those kind of entities are certainly not a plaything Luna can toy with without a serious chance for being found out and nasty blowback. Even if she is a rank 10 spirit, that'd be like saying a rank 5 spirit carelessly toying with a rank 3 spirit could never go wrong. Or a Master mage using a Disciple as his plaything is not playing with fire. Sure you're a master, good for you, but a Disciple can still fuck you up if he catches you on the backfoot (or has luck in a clash of wills) or he could rain ruination upon your schemes while you're otherwise engaged or... You can do that (and so could Luna, I'm sure), but it's certainly not something Luna does all the time to all of them casually. Pretty sure she's too good a trickster to be that careless and got at least a rudimentary survival instinct.<br /> <br /> All of this aside, Luna (and earlier Father Wolf) sound like they would be the primary sponsors of Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-24-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T11:47:44-07:00","id":1133479,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a>: you read way, way too much into my 7 word post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T05:17:58-07:00","id":1133741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133446#post1133446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but Archmages are still super powerful entities. No need to defend other splats in the Mage forum. It gets old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as vampire is my favorite game, I kind of have to agree. The devs outright stated that mages are so powerful because the horror of mage is hubris and seeing what happens when you give some random person god-like powers.<br /> <br /> I think the sponsor bit is a bit neat though, so let me provide what could be the vampire's sponsor: The Blood.<br /> <br /> In one excerpt from vampire 2e, one Kindred notes how there are so many variations to their kind: there are the various clans and bloodlines, the kindred and the strix, dhampir, and each covenant brings something new to the Kindred condition (I provided more examples than the excerpt).<br /> <br /> The kindred was clearly a paranoid wreck by the time you got to the end of the excerpt, but I always found the idea of The Blood (as said Kindred put it) of being alive, and at least somewhat sentient if it is trying to evolve, to be kind of interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T05:20:52-07:00","id":1133743,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> Luna is a Rank seven or eight entity, if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T05:42:49-07:00","id":1133749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133741#post1133741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the sponsor bit is a bit neat though, so let me provide what could be the vampire's sponsor: The Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would probably &quot;just&quot; be a possible form for the 'God of vampirism' mentioned before. A highlevel spiritual shadow of the shared trait of kindred clans and bloodlines, Vitae.<br /> <br /> Strix however are another shoe entirely. I think it's been said somewhere that their home dimension is a lower depth and I don't think entities from there actually create spirits. An alternative to the Spirit (as in denizen of the shadow) as a Patron a godlike entity from this lower depth that somehow has major influence in the fallen world could be (one of) the Partron entity(s).<br /> <br /> In the end a supernatural splat doesn't have to be the providence of a singular entity. Personally when playing mage (and your chronicle is crazy enough these questions become relevant IC) it can be tempting to attribute them to a specific Archmaster or one of the Exarchs (like I like to do with the Psychopomp for Vampires), but in the end it doesn't have to be a monopol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T05:54:06-07:00","id":1133753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133749#post1133749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would probably &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; be a possible form for the 'God of vampirism' mentioned before. A highlevel spiritual shadow of the shared trait of kindred clans and bloodlines, Vitae.<br /> <br /> Strix however are another shoe entirely. I think it's been said somewhere that their home dimension is a lower depth and I don't think entities from there actually create spirits. An alternative to the Spirit (as in denizen of the shadow) as a Patron a godlike entity from this lower depth that somehow has major influence in the fallen world could be (one of) the Partron entity(s).<br /> <br /> In the end a supernatural splat doesn't have to be the providence of a singular entity. Personally when playing mage (and your chronicle is crazy enough these questions become relevant IC) it can be tempting to attribute them to a specific Archmaster or one of the Exarchs (like I like to do with the Psychopomp for Vampires), but in the end it doesn't have to be a monopol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's definitely a group by group basis. I could see at least one of the Exarchs being a sponsor for the kindred because Kindred help keep up the Lie for their own Masquerade, albeit unintentionally.<br /> <br /> Of course, I think it should be noted that vampires in 2e might not care if Ted down the street believes in monsters; I think they'll just keep an eye on him in the event that Ted realizes that the people down the street are the monsters. So, that might be a dent in the Masquerade upholding the Lie bit.<br /> <br /> But I think as interesting as that bit could be, I think some people (myself included) prefer the sponsor to be something that is somewhat related to the splat because it feels a bit more personal. <br /> <br /> Though a Tremere Archmage would fit the personal bit because vampires and strix were mentioned in their legacy write up in 1e, if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T06:05:17-07:00","id":1133757,"title":"","content":"My reasoning for Exarcharial patronage of vampirism is slightly different, see below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1125609#post1125609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my personal headcanon vampires (as far as MtAw games are concerned, I wouldn't run it that way in a VtR game) have been created by the Psychopomp as a means of stifling humanities potential to awaken. Vampires still have souls, but they're crippled things, unable to awaken and they infect those they feed upon with a little bit of themselves. Sure you can still awaken even if you're being fed from regularily by vampires but in my personal headcanon the chances decrease (and are really small for ghouls).</div> </div> </div> </div>That said I think it depends on the theme of the chronicle who should or should not be the sponsor. If I rand VtR and this question was of any relevance (I really don't see how a vampire game could ever get there to be honest... but who knows, prove me wrong!) I'd most definitly not throw in Archmages or worse Exarchs. They do nothing for the themes of Vampire. In a mage game on the other hand I can see Silver Ladder mages fervently defending the theory that Terata in general are part of an exarcharial plot to cripple individual souls and haven them cripple others too due to their parasitic feeding practices. The truth may of course be very different... or at lest far more layered.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Focus shouldn't be on which supernatural splat has the biggest dick or wether another splat is diminished by archmages meddling. This question demands an individual awnser for each campaign that suits the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:28:02-07:00","id":1133849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133743#post1133743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> Luna is a Rank seven or eight entity, if memory serves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstborns are 7; Celestines are 8-9, 10 is beyond perceived conception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T16:59:17-07:00","id":1133992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133749#post1133749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would probably &quot;just&quot; be a possible form for the 'God of vampirism' mentioned before. A highlevel spiritual shadow of the shared trait of kindred clans and bloodlines, Vitae.<br /> <br /> Strix however are another shoe entirely. I think it's been said somewhere that their home dimension is a lower depth and I don't think entities from there actually create spirits. An alternative to the Spirit (as in denizen of the shadow) as a Patron a godlike entity from this lower depth that somehow has major influence in the fallen world could be (one of) the Partron entity(s).<br /> <br /> In the end a supernatural splat doesn't have to be the providence of a singular entity. Personally when playing mage (and your chronicle is crazy enough these questions become relevant IC) it can be tempting to attribute them to a specific Archmaster or one of the Exarchs (like I like to do with the Psychopomp for Vampires), but in the end it doesn't have to be a monopol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, if I was going to have the Blood act as a sponser for vampires I would have it be its own entity, something entirely different from spirits, gods or anything else, something unique with unknown origins and strange goals. I would also make it so that the players are never entirely sure if it is a sentient thing, or simply a force acting in the only way it can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T17:38:59-07:00","id":1134000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1133992#post1133992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, if I was going to have the Blood act as a sponser for vampires I would have it be its own entity, something entirely different from spirits, gods or anything else, something unique with unknown origins and strange goals. I would also make it so that the players are never entirely sure if it is a sentient thing, or simply a force acting in the only way it can.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's generally going to be the way I'll roll with it if it ever comes up. I liked the idea of the Curse/Blood of being this eldritch thing that's been around awhile. Whether it's actually sentient, or what we would consider sentient, is up to debate. Course, that's probably going to be if I do crossover, or just for vampire (and how the Ascension War would come up in vampire alone, I don't know). Otherwise, I try to stick to the same cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T04:21:12-07:00","id":1134431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121444#post1121444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would an Arch master level Chronicle even look like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s3lA6abQprM\" data-code=\"s3lA6abQprM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/s3lA6abQprM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T07:53:55-07:00","id":1135151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120687-archmages-vs-other-supernaturals?p=1121675#post1121675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before counting Elder Vampires out remember this: Nothing in Imperial Mysteries says Archmasters can't be blood bound.<br /> <br /> Also fun side note: A personal favorite fan theory if mine is that the Fog of Eternity isn't so much Kindred Elders going senile, but Elders retaining the memory of their previous incarnations before an Archmage reality edits. That way it seems like they remember things that didn't happen, but really they're remembering things that no longer happened. Fun food for thought. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a fun theory and one that I'd thought of as well. There are some real questions about what happens to memory when a rewrite hits, after all.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}